ears)","anomalies from the calendar-month normal; Sen's slope, Mann-Kendall (Yue-Wang), OLS with effective sample size (trend_stats.py)"],"synthetic":false,"caveat":"Data: NASA CERES SYN1deg, built from satellite measurements, about 100 km squares (averaged into 2° squares; coastal squares include some sea). The trend is a straight line through 2001–2025; it shows what changed, not why. The record is 25 years long, shorter than the 30 years usually used to describe a climate."}}